(:spec :id gatewayConfig :v 2 :date "2026-09-25" :file "~/.asl/gateway.asn" :reader "bin/asl-gateway gateway_config_parse" :check "bin/asl-gateway config check [file]"
  :doc "routing config for bin/asl-gateway, per user, never in a repo. A file without :v 2 is read as v1 (work/GWN/profiles.asn: :profiles of :routes with :models strings) and keeps working unchanged; a missing file means the built-in v1 default"
  :shape "(:gateway :v 2 :providers (PROVIDER ...) :models (MODEL ...) :intents (INTENT ...) :profiles (PROFILE ...) :uses (USE ...))"
  :codeRoute "(:codeRoute :id ID :writer ALIAS :retries 0..2 :escalate ALIAS :retryWriter ALIAS(optional, retries go to it instead of :writer) :escalateTimeoutSec S :escalateRetries 0..5 :escalateRetryStatuses (CODE ...)) rows under :codeRoutes; writer asks the alias, a caller gate checks, the raw gate error is fed back up to :retries times, then one escalation to the :escalate alias with the same error, then stop; aliases only, temperature from the alias row (CAL/ensemble-20261028.asn variant d)"
  :provider "(:provider :id ID :kind openai|cli :base URL :keyEnv ENVNAME :sessionHeader HEADERNAME :timeoutSec N :rpm N); built-in ids agy codex claude (cli) and gemini groq openrouter ollama (openai) need no entry, and an entry with a built-in id overrides its fields; a key is named by :keyEnv only, a :key field is an error; :sessionHeader names an upstream header (an http token, letters digits and hyphens) that carries the caller's X-ASL-Session id, for a provider that keys routing or caching off a stable per-conversation id (e.g. OpenCode's x-opencode-session); absent means no such header is sent; :assistantReasoning true adds reasoning_content \"\" to each assistant message that has no thinking field (ifm answers 400 to multi-turn history without one), default false"
  :model "(:model :id ALIAS :provider ID :name \"upstream name\" :calibration \"registry id\" :temperature X :effort low|medium|high|xhigh|none :maxTokens N :timeoutSec N :reasoning true|false :rpm N :api chat|responses); :api responses sends the upstream body {model, input, instructions?, max_output_tokens?} to POST <base>/responses and converts the Responses reply into the chat shape, default chat; :rpm on the alias or its provider paces requests per upstream model locally, absent means no local pacing (a 429 moves to the next chain entry); params on the alias override the registry row named by :calibration (asl/grammar/calibration.asn)"
  :intent "(:intent :id ID :as PARENT); a request intent (X-ASL-Intent or body intent) matches the route for itself, else for its parent, and so on, else the :intent any route; an intent named only by :as is declared too"
  :profile "(:profile :id ID :routes ((:intent ID|any :chain (ALIAS ...)) ...) :fallback PROFILE); a chain entry is an alias, or a string read as a v1 model name"
  :mode "(:profile ... :mode pin|route|judge :judge (:empty true|false :truncated true|false :stepIntents (INTENT ...) :stepHeads (\"TEXT\" ...))), default route: pin tries only the first member of the matched route (no spread, affinity reorder, later member or fallback profile) and relays that member's HTTP error with its own status and headers, Retry-After included, while auth, accounting, limits, buckets and breakers still apply; route is the chain, spread, limits and breakers as before; judge is route where a 200 reply that fails a check is charged to its member as judge:CHECK and the next member is tried: empty (message content blank before any reasoning salvage, no tool calls; default true), truncated (finish_reason length; default true), noStepForm (the request intent is in :stepIntents, default none, and the answer holds none of :stepHeads, default (\"(:step\")); an HTTP error moves on in route and judge alike; a second-model cross-check is not a gateway mode"
  :use "(:use :for NAME :profile ID); :for default is the default profile; X-ASL-Use NAME picks another"
  :select "X-ASL-Profile, else X-ASL-Use through :uses, else env ASL_GATEWAY_PROFILE, else the default use; an unknown profile or use answers 400"
  :route "a request whose model is empty, default or profile tries its route's chain strictly in order, then the :fallback profile's route for the same intent, and so on; an alias already tried is skipped; an HTTP error, a Gemini rate-limit bucket miss, a CLI failure or an empty reply moves to the next entry; no model outside the config is tried, and when all fail the reply is 502 naming the aliases"
  :waits "top-level (:gateway ... :bucketWaitSec S :queueBudgetSec S): :bucketWaitSec (default 5) is how long a chain member before the last waits for its rpm bucket; :queueBudgetSec (default 30) is how long the last member waits for its bucket when the caller gave no queue budget (X-ASL-Queue-Ms, X-ASL-Queue-Timeout or body queue_timeout win); still refused, the request ends 429 with Retry-After; a non-positive value is a warning and the default stays; :queueBudgetSec above 3600 is out of range (an error in config check, the default 30 at runtime)"
  :busyRetry "top-level (:gateway ... :busyRetrySec N): the Retry-After seconds on a 503 the gateway makes itself when a retry soon is the right answer (an endpoint that went away, one that did not warm within coldStartMs, no endpoint admitted); 1..3600, default 1 adopted; outside the range is an error in config check and the default at runtime"
  :cooldowns "top-level (:gateway ... :breakerCooldownSec S :cooldown429Sec S :cooldown429MaxSec S :cooldownSlackSec S :parkMaxSec S): an account-wide failure (401, 402, a provider-wide quota body) or three 503s open the provider or the member for :breakerCooldownSec (default 600); a 429 that is not a daily cap opens only that member, for the wait its Retry-After or x-ratelimit-reset* headers name, else to the end of the current minute plus :cooldownSlackSec (default 1, never over 60 s) when the member is paced by :rpm, else for :cooldown429Sec (default 15) doubled on each further 429 in a row up to :cooldown429MaxSec (default 600); a daily cap, or a monthly usage limit on the whole provider, parks until its provider's reset (a monthly limit with no reset hint until the next month start at 00:00 UTC), never longer than :parkMaxSec (default 2764800, 32 days); a success ends the streak"
  :temperatureFixed "(:model ... :temperatureFixed F): the gateway always sends temperature F to this model, whatever the request, an X-ASL-Temperature header or the route says (Kimi accepts 1 only and answers 400 to anything else); a cascade fallback model keeps the request temperature; :temperatureFixed together with :temperature on one row, or a non-number, is a config error"
  :affinity "top-level (:gateway ... :affinity true|false :affinityStickSec S :affinityForgetSec S :affinitySwitch dropReasoning|keep), defaults true, 1800, 86400, dropReasoning: a session (X-ASL-Session unless it is the server's asl-run-* fallback, else body session) goes first to the member that last answered it while that answer is under :affinityStickSec old, in every route and after the :spread order, and breakers, limits and buckets still skip that member when it is down; when another member answers, the forwarded transcript loses the reasoning_content, reasoning, reasoning_details and thinking fields and the thinking or reasoning content blocks of every assistant message unless :affinitySwitch is keep; a record older than :affinityForgetSec is forgotten; :affinity false sticks, drops and records nothing; the rows are read from the loaded config on every request"
  :limits "top-level (:gateway ... :limits ((:limit :scope account|group|model|endpoint :provider P :model M :group G :endpoint URL :window minute|hour|fiveHour|day|week|month :calls N :tokens N :tokensIn N :tokensOut N :tokensCached N :usd X :concurrency N) ...)): a call is charged to every row whose scope contains it and the tightest budget binds (the row used up the furthest skips the member with limit:WINDOW; none spent, the calendar window furthest ahead of an even spread plus a tenth paces with pace:WINDOW); account counts every alias of :provider, model one alias (:model) of :provider, group the aliases of the (:group) row named by :group, endpoint every provider whose :base equals :endpoint; :tokens counts input plus output, :tokensIn, :tokensOut and :tokensCached one kind, :usd the cost at the models' :priceInPerM and :priceOutPerM (a model with no price costs 0), and every unit is a cap over :window, 0 or absent meaning that unit is not limited; :concurrency N (1..1024, no window needed) admits N calls in flight under the row and parks the N+1th, which sleeps :concurrencyPollMs and asks again until its queue budget is used up and is then skipped with limit:concurrency; only the last member of a chain parks, an earlier full member is skipped at once with limit:concurrency so a later member can answer; an error in config check: an unknown scope or window, a row without a unit, a negative cap, :concurrency out of range, a limit row naming a group that is not declared. Example shapes, not live rows: per-model separate budgets (SUB-OFFER-90) are one (:limit :provider P :scope model :model M :window month :calls N) per model; a plan quota shared by all of a provider's models is one (:limit :provider P :scope account :window fiveHour :calls N)"
  :requests "top-level (:gateway ... :requestDeadlineSec N): every accepted request gets an id, an accepted row and, where its connection closes, exactly one done row (outcome ok, limit, noRoute, timeout, upstreamError, gatewayError or clientGone) in gatewayRequests.asn under .asl/run/usage; at server start an accepted row with no done row becomes a done row with outcome lost; gateway status lists requests older than :requestDeadlineSec (1..86400, default 900) as stuck and the lost ones of the last 24 hours; /hub/status shows :requests and :stuck"
  :groups "top-level (:gateway ... :groups ((:group :id G :provider P :models (ALIAS ...)) ...)): the listed aliases of provider P share every limit row that names the group, so a plan quota shared across its models or a free-tier daily count across all free models is one budget; an error in config check: no :id, a duplicate :id, no :provider or :models, a model that is not a model of that provider"
  :concurrency "top-level (:gateway ... :concurrencyLeaseSec S :concurrencyPollMs MS): :concurrencyLeaseSec (default 600 adopted, 10..86400) is how long a call may hold a concurrency slot before the gateway treats it as lost and frees it; :concurrencyPollMs (default 250 adopted, 10..5000) is how often a parked call asks again; out of range is an error in config check and the default at runtime"
  :prices "(:model ... :priceInPerM X :priceOutPerM X): dollars per million input and output tokens of this model, used only by :usd limit units; absent means the model costs 0 there"
  :ledger "top-level (:gateway ... :ledgerMaxBytes N :ledgerKeep N): every upstream attempt, ok or failed, appends one row to the usage ledger (usage/gatewayCalls.asn) with provider, alias, model, outcome, the HTTP :status (absent when there was no answer) and for a failure a redacted :reason; at :ledgerMaxBytes (default 10485760) the file moves to gatewayCalls.asn.N, N one above the newest kept, and only the newest :ledgerKeep (default 8) generations stay; readers see the kept generations and the live file, a window read opening older generations only as far back as its window"
  :params "effort from the alias or registry always applies; temperature, maxTokens and timeoutSec apply unless the request sets X-ASL-Temperature, ASL_TEMPERATURE, body temperature, body max_tokens, X-ASL-Timeout or body timeout; :reasoning true raises an unset max_tokens to the reasoning floor"
  :observe "/health JSON gateway and ASN :gateway carry :uses, every profile and every alias with its resolved params and the registry path; the selected :profile carries :v 2 :routes :fallback"
  :learn "top-level (:gateway ... :learnRamp true|false :learnRampPct N :learnWindows NAMES): bin/asl gateway learn reads the usage ledger and keeps, per provider and per alias and per window, the most sent calls and tokens reached with no upstream 429 and the fewest calls at the first 429 (learned.asn under .asl/run/usage, a peak is never lowered, our own refusals count for nothing); with :learnRamp true (default false) or --ramp one pass raises a configured account or model call cap that the provider was driven up to with no 429 ever seen by :learnRampPct percent (5..100, default 25, at least 1) into learnedCaps.asn, and the gateway judges calls against those caps only while :learnRamp is true; the same pass raises a per-model :rpm bucket (not a provider shared one) that our own bucket refused while no 429 was ever seen for the model, by the same percent up to 8 times the configured rate, into learnedRpm.asn, never lowering it; :learnWindows (default all five) are resolved to a quarter of the window"
  :checkRules ("unknown alias, provider, fallback profile, use profile or route intent is an error" "a cycle in intent parents or profile fallbacks is an error" "a key env var that is unset is a warning naming the var, never a value" "a :calibration id absent from the registry is a warning" "a non-positive :bucketWaitSec or :queueBudgetSec is a warning and keeps the default" "a :queueBudgetSec above 3600 or a :busyRetrySec outside 1..3600 is an error in config check; serve keeps the default" "a :learnRamp that is not true or false, a :learnRampPct outside 5..100 or a :learnWindows naming a window other than minute hour fiveHour day week is an error in config check" "a :cooldown429Sec outside 1..3600, a :cooldown429MaxSec outside 1..90000 or under :cooldown429Sec, or a :cooldownSlackSec outside 0..30, or a :parkMaxSec outside 60..2764800, a :ledgerMaxBytes outside 65536..1073741824 or a :ledgerKeep outside 1..64 is an error in config check; serve keeps the default" "an :affinity that is not true or false, an :affinityStickSec outside 1..86400, an :affinityForgetSec outside 1..604800 or under :affinityStickSec, or an :affinitySwitch other than dropReasoning or keep is an error in config check" "a profile :mode other than pin, route or judge, an unknown :judge key, a non-boolean :judge :empty or :truncated, or a :judge :stepIntents or :stepHeads that is not a list is an error")
  :receipt "(:configCheck :file PATH :v 1|2 :registry PATH :status :ok|:error :errors (STRING ...) :warnings (STRING ...) :profiles N :models N :uses N); exit 1 when :errors is not empty")
